{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790714943,"nonce":"+MKZ213FCdV04KmNJIKkDJL/h+4=","title":"Register reflection metadata for extern Math","message":"Math is an extern standard-library class whose methods lower to native intrinsics. It has no MIR struct, so the normal class RTTI walk never registers it. Type.getClassName(Math) and Type.resolveClass(\"Math\") both returned null; TestReflect first failed at Math after the preceding Xml dependency fix.\n\nThe Cranelift runtime-class fallback now registers Math under the stable class ID when no source-backed entry exists. It includes the static fields declared by Math.hx so Type.getClassFields(Math) exposes the same API. haxe-conformance/regressions/MathTypeReflection.hx fails before the change and passes afterward. TestReflect advances to unit.MyEnum, which is a separate enum reflection failure.\n\nValidation: authored regression suite, compiler Clippy, targeted rustfmt, and full tiered conformance. Workspace-wide fmt reports unrelated staged GPU files.","files":null}]}